+# Local, rmw_tickle-specific patch (not upstream) - see rmw_tickle/PLAN.md's own Milestone for
+# this (the follow-up to Milestones 39/41/42, un-excluding this file from test_msgs_rmw_tickle.
+# patch's own generation list). Every unbounded '<Type>[] field' here (no ROS 2 upper bound of its
+# own) hits the same limitation rcl_interfaces_rmw_tickle.patch's own header comment (see its
+# SetParameters.srv) already documents in full: adapt.py's own auto-derived capacity never applies
+# to a string-element array, or an array of a nested message type that is itself not fixed-size -
+# both permanent, by-design limits, not gaps expected to close. With every field here being one or
+# the other (or, for the plain-scalar arrays, simply not the struct's own trailing field, since
+# many other arrays follow each one), none can auto-derive regardless - every field gets the same
+# explicit '# @capacity 3' annotation, matching this file's own sibling fixed/bounded-array test
+# files (Arrays.msg's own '[3]', BoundedSequences.msg's own '[<=3]') for consistency, not a real
+# workload's own batch size.
